<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 October, from 451 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/451">451 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,575 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Chalcedon opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> summoned by Emperor Marcian met at Chalcedon, across the Bosporus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Its definition of Christ as one person in two natures became orthodoxy in the West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> but split the eastern churches.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">876 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,150 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis the Younger defeats Charles the Bald at Andernach</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andernach">Andernach</a>, the East Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger">Louis the Younger</a> defeated his uncle, the West Frankish king and emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, who had tried to seize the western lands of Louis's inheritance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger">Louis the Younger</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1200">1200 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">826 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isabella of Angoulême is crowned queen of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-of-angouleme">Isabella of Angoulême</a>, heiress of the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angouleme">Angoulême</a> and second wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a>, was crowned queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. The marriage provoked the Lusignans and helped bring on the loss of Normandy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-of-angouleme">Isabella of Angoulême</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1480">1480 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">546 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Stand on the Ugra River begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhmat-khan">Akhmat Khan</a> of the Great Horde began a stand-off on opposite banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ugra-river">Ugra River</a>. The Horde withdrew without a decisive battle, traditionally marking the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> overlordship over Muscovy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-stand-on-the-ugra-river">Great Stand on the Ugra River</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1856">1856 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chinese officials board the Arrow at Canton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Qing officials boarded the Arrow, a Chinese-owned ship flying a British flag, and arrested its crew on suspicion of piracy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> used the incident as grounds for the Second Opium War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Chicago Fire breaks out</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire broke out in a barn on DeKoven Street and, driven by strong winds, burned for two days across Chicago. About 300 people died and 100,000 lost their homes, but rebuilding made the city a centre of modern architecture.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Corporal Alvin York captures 132 German soldiers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Argonne Forest, Corporal Alvin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> led a small patrol that silenced German machine guns, killing about 25 soldiers and taking 132 prisoners. He received the Medal of Honor and became a national hero.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Che Guevara is captured in Bolivia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolivian troops, aided by the CIA, wounded and captured Ernesto 'Che' Guevara in the Yuro ravine. He was executed the next day at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-higuera">La Higuera</a>, and his image became an enduring icon of revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li></ol>
