<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 8 October <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jacqueline-countess-of-hainaut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jacqueline-countess-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jacqueline, Countess of Hainaut</span><span class="tp">1401–1436</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-george-i-elector-of-saxony"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-george-i-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John George I, Elector of Saxony</span><span class="tp">1585–1656</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-fielding"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-fielding.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry Fielding</span><span class="tp">1707–1754</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-odonoju"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-odonoju.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan O'Donojú</span><span class="tp">1762–1821</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/miguel-grau-seminario"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/miguel-grau-seminario.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Miguel Grau Seminario</span><span class="tp">1834–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-monash"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-monash.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Monash</span><span class="tp">1865–1931</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/clement-attlee"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/clement-attlee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Clement Attlee</span><span class="tp">1883–1967</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
